# Rolling window, not an archive. An entry stays only until every machine has
# applied it once; then it is dropped, so a later file may reuse the name
# without an apply silently deleting it. Add an entry when a managed path is
# retired, and clear it after the last machine has caught up.

# The mandatory skill-evaluation preamble is withdrawn. The hook shipped for
# months without a UserPromptSubmit registration, so nothing fired it; left on
# disk it is a live executable that a stale or re-added registration reaches,
# injecting a skill roll-call and a tool-routing table into every prompt.
.claude/hooks/user-prompt-skill-eval.sh

# The brief re-anchored a writing-style rule at the point of use. The style is
# empty now, so the file restates nothing and its one reader inlines the shape
# instead. Left on disk it is an unreachable document.
.claude/shared/decision-brief.md

# Focus Notify is installed from its upstream source now. Remove the managed
# local reimplementation before Herdr enables the replacement, or both event
# hooks can produce the same notification.
.config/herdr/plugins/herdr-focus-notify

# se-doc-review and se-plan are retired: they wrap ce-doc-review and ce-plan,
# which are outside the installed compound engineering set. Deleting their
# sources left the deployed copies discoverable, so agents still invoked them
# and launched peers against a skill that does not exist.
.agents/skills/se-doc-review
.agents/skills/se-plan
.claude/skills/se-doc-review
.claude/skills/se-plan
